<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="about-wrap">

      <figure class="about-photo fade-in">
        <img src="/assets/dr-phillips.jpg" alt="Dr. Matthew Phillips, DDS — founder of 3rd Set Smiles in Tempe, Arizona" width="1120" height="928">
        <figcaption class="about-photo-info">
          <h3>Dr. Matthew Phillips</h3>
          <p>DDS &middot; Founder, 3rd Set Smiles</p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="about-content prose">
        <div class="fade-in">
          <p class="about-tagline">Advanced surgical skill, a soldier&rsquo;s discipline, and a genuine belief in second chances.</p>

          <p>Dr. Matthew Phillips grew up in Mesa, Arizona, graduated from Mesa&rsquo;s Mountain View High School in 1994, and never really left the Valley behind. <!-- Confirmed by Mark 2026-09-30: raised in Mesa; Mountain View High School (Mesa), class of 1994. --> For dental school he headed east to the New York University College of Dentistry, where he received his Doctorate of Dental Surgery in 2004. <!-- Confirmed by Mark 2026-09-30: NYU DDS 2004 is his only degree. Prior BYU/ASU coursework is intentionally not listed. --> More than two decades later, his experience runs the full length of the field &mdash; from everyday family checkups to some of the most complex full-arch implant reconstruction in modern dentistry.</p>

          <p>He founded 3rd Set Smiles in Tempe to practice the way he always believed dentistry should be done: unhurried, honest, and built entirely around the person in the chair. Cleanings, fillings, and crowns; simple or complex extractions, implants, and dentures &mdash; fixed and removable &mdash; comprehensive care under one roof, explained in plain language, with no pressure and no sales pitch.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>A Decade in the U.S. Army</h2>
          <p>Dr. Phillips served ten years as a dentist in the United States Army, caring for soldiers and their families through assignments in South Korea, Iraq, Hawaii, and Maryland. <!-- CONFIRM: total years of service and list of duty stations. --> Along the way he completed three years of advanced surgical training and developed a focus on implant dentistry and rebuilding smiles for patients with severe tooth loss &mdash; often far from the comfort of a private office. He separated from the Army as a Major with an honorable discharge, and was recognized with the Brigadier General Joseph L. Bernier Award for his contributions to the Army&rsquo;s trauma research. <!-- CONFIRM: length of surgical training program; final rank (Major) and discharge type; Bgen Joseph L. Bernier Award. --></p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in callout-box">
          <p>He didn&rsquo;t just learn full-arch implant surgery at the highest level &mdash; he went on to teach it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>Teaching the Next Generation of Implant Dentists</h2>
          <p>After his military career, Dr. Phillips refined his expertise in advanced implant techniques &mdash; including All-on-4&reg; and implant-retained dentures &mdash; and stepped into a role teaching others. As Surgical Training Advisor at Renew Anchored Dentures, founded by ClearChoice co-founder Dr. Don Miloni, he helped establish surgical protocols and trained practicing dentists in full-arch implant procedures. <!-- CONFIRM: exact title (Surgical Training Advisor / Director of Surgical Services) and tenure dates at Renew. --> The same hands that trained other clinicians in full-arch protocols now care for patients here in Tempe.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>Education &amp; Credentials</h2>
          <ul class="credential-list">
            <li>Doctorate of Dental Surgery (DDS) &mdash; New York University College of Dentistry, 2004 <!-- Confirmed by Mark 2026-09-30. --></li>
            <li>U.S. Army Dental Corps &mdash; three years of advanced surgical training <!-- CONFIRM: name of program (AEGD, oral surgery rotation, etc.) and completion year. --></li>
            <li>Surgical Training Advisor &mdash; Renew Anchored Dentures <!-- CONFIRM: exact title and tenure dates. --></li>
            <li>Member &mdash; International Congress of Oral Implantologists (ICOI) <!-- CONFIRM: current ICOI membership. --></li>
            <li>Brigadier General Joseph L. Bernier Award &mdash; U.S. Army trauma research contributions <!-- CONFIRM: award name and year. --></li>
            <li>Published in the Journal of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery, 2010 <!-- CONFIRM: publication and year. --></li>
            <li>Licensed in Arizona <!-- CONFIRM: AZ license number and status. --></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>Why &ldquo;3rd Set Smiles&rdquo;?</h2>
          <p>Dr. Phillips loves tennis, and the name started there &mdash; in a best-of-three match, the third set is where it all comes down to the finish. He worked a dental meaning into it too: most of us get two sets of teeth, baby teeth and adult teeth. For patients who have lost theirs, <a href="/services/dental-implants/">dental implants</a> and <a href="/services/all-on-4/">All-on-4</a> full-arch treatment can be a third set, and a second chance at a confident smile.</p>
          <!-- Confirmed by Mark 2026-09-30: Dr. Phillips likes tennis; the name is a tennis reference with the dental angle (a 3rd set of teeth from All-on-4 / dental implants) worked in. -->
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>His Approach to Care</h2>
          <p>Dr. Phillips believes most dental decisions are bigger than a single tooth &mdash; they&rsquo;re about how you eat, speak, sleep, and feel about yourself. Every consultation begins with a real conversation: what brought you in, what you&rsquo;ve tried before, and what you actually want the outcome to look like. He believes deeply in second chances, and in making every patient feel genuinely welcome &mdash; no judgment about how long it&rsquo;s been, and never any pressure to commit on the spot.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>A Heart for Veterans</h2>
          <p>As a veteran himself, Dr. Phillips has a particular commitment to those who have worn the uniform. 3rd Set Smiles is proud to be a veteran-owned practice, and to offer special consideration for veterans without dental insurance. <a href="/veterans/">Learn more about our care for veterans →</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in">
          <h2>Beyond the Office</h2>
          <p>Outside the practice, Dr. Phillips is a lifelong Arizonan and a proud Army veteran &mdash; happiest when he&rsquo;s given someone a reason to smile again. Today he&rsquo;s raising his own family here in Mesa, so the East Valley isn&rsquo;t just where he works &mdash; it&rsquo;s home.</p>
          <!-- Confirmed by Mark 2026-09-30: family lives in Mesa. Deliberately does NOT name his children or the school they attend (privacy/safety for minors). -->
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in pull-quote">
          <p>&ldquo;I listen first, examine second, and only then talk about treatment. People deserve honest answers &mdash; not a sales pitch.&rdquo;</p>
          <cite>&mdash; Dr. Matthew Phillips, DDS, Founder</cite>
        </div>

        <div class="fade-in btn-row" style="margin-top:32px">
          {{ bookingCta(booking, "Book with Dr. Matthew Phillips", { scope: "provider", source: "provider_profile", aria: "Book online with Dr. Matthew Phillips on Zocdoc" }) }}
